## Summary

I shipped a production-polished, Apple-idiomatic **`Pagination`** shared surface at `apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/Pagination.*` — the native SwiftUI parity of `web/src/components/ui/Pagination.tsx`, following the established house pattern (AiUsageCard/ToolCard).

**8 surface files** (Model, Adapter, Chrome, Views, entry, Previews, Tests, strings):
- **Parity**: web arithmetic reproduced verbatim (`totalPages = max(1, ceil(total/pageSize))`, start/end window with the `total==0 → 0` ternary, prev/first disabled `page≤1`, next/last disabled `page≥totalPages`, un-grouped i18next numbers). "Showing X–Y of Z" line, rows-per-page `Picker` (web `<select>`), First/Prev/indicator/Next/Last cluster, RTL-mirroring SF Symbol chevrons, responsive `ViewThatFits` (`flex-col sm:flex-row`).
- **State-holder seam** (P1/S8 `PaginationSource` + `@Observable` model) keeps the controlled-component contract; **every state renders** (loading skeleton, empty = web zero chrome + "No results", error+retry, data, inline stale/offline freshness chip+banner with one-shot auto-refresh).
- **i18n** via per-surface "Pagination" table (no English literals in code), **P1/S9 tokens**, full **a11y** labels, **P1/S11** `view.opened` telemetry.
- Established `TeslaSync/shared-surfaces` and wired it into `project.yml` (iOS+macOS) and `.swiftlint.yml`.

**Verification — green on every host-runnable gate:** swiftformat `0/7`, swiftlint --strict `0` violations in the 8 files (the 1 whole-app violation is pre-existing in `LifetimeStatsWidget.Adapter.swift`), placeholder scan `0/0`, xcodegen enumerates all 8 files, and an **isolated SwiftPM build of the exact shipped sources against the real design system under Swift 6 strict concurrency with 63/63 runtime assertions passing**.

